# Skipped macros (no Bazel equivalent needed):
#
# configure.ac:
#   AC_ARG_ENABLE([gcc-warnings]) (line 90) - the port silences every
#     warning via COPTS instead, so the -W flag battery has no effect.
#   AM_GNU_GETTEXT([external]) (line 118) - there is no gettext module in
#     the BCR, so NLS is always off and LIBINTL is empty.
#   AM_CONDITIONAL([USE_INCLUDED_REGEX]) (line 127) - rules_cc_autoconf's
#     gnulib/m4/regex pins ac_use_included_regex=yes, matching grep's own
#     default, so there is nothing left to toggle.
#   gl_EARLY / gl_INIT (lines 51, 120) - expanded by GNULIB_M4_DEPS.
#   AC_CONFIG_FILES / AC_OUTPUT (lines 214-237) - the Makefile.in ->
#     Makefile expansion has no analogue here.
#   gl_cv_func_mbrtowc_empty_input / gl_cv_func_mbrlen_empty_input
#     (lines 70-71) - configure.ac pre-seeds these to skip AC_RUN_IFELSE
#     probes; rules_cc_autoconf reaches the same answers without running
